<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A vocabulary DECLARATION's range must CONTAIN the constructs it contains.

  M60 containment ledger, finding: `src/ast/real-xml-analyzer.ts` anchored a declaration's
  symbol range to the `name=` Attribute node whenever the value shared the attribute's line.
  That is the right LINE and the wrong SPAN, and `contains` is made of spans:

    <xsd:complexType name="Address">     symbol `Address` @ name="Address"
      <xsd:sequence>                     symbol `xsd:sequence` @ <xsd:sequence>...

  produced the edge `Address -contains-> xsd:sequence` — which is TRUE — with a target that
  is not inside its source, and the attribute symbol `name` occupied the identical byte
  range as the declaration itself. Measured over 400 corpus files: 253 byte ranges held by
  two distinct names, and 474 of 4,383 `contains` edges whose containment claim no span can
  express. Both are invisible to a resolution rate, which is 100 % on this type.

  Three shapes are pinned, because the fix is PARTIAL and each shape is a different
  decision. The rule is "anchor the ELEMENT when the tag, the `name=` attribute and its
  value all share one line" — the only shape in which the element's row and the
  attribute's row are the same row, and therefore the only one where moving the anchor
  cannot move the reported LINE.

    shape 1  lines 31-35, tag/attribute/value all on one line -> anchor the ELEMENT, so
             `Address` at 1818..1963 contains `name` at 1835..1849, `xsd:sequence` at
             1855..1942 and `street` at 1876..1922
    shape 2  lines 36-38, the attribute on the NEXT line     -> anchor the Attribute, and
             the reported line stays 37, the line the name is written on
    shape 3  lines 39-41, the value on a line of its own      -> anchor the AttValue, and
             the reported line stays 40

  Shapes 2 and 3 keep the old anchor, so their containment stays unverifiable by span: on
  shape 3 the `name` Attribute node at 2055..2084 ENCLOSES the declaration at 2067..2084,
  which is why `ValueOnNextLine -contains-> name` is a true edge with an inverted range
  order. That is the declared cost of the fix, pinned here so it cannot be quietly
  forgotten: if a future change anchors shapes 2 and 3 to the element, both symbols report
  the TAG's line and this fixture fails.
-->
<xsd:schema xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" targetNamespace="urn:example:containment">
  <xsd:complexType name="Address">
    <xsd:sequence>
      <xsd:element name="street" type="xsd:string"/>
    </xsd:sequence>
  </xsd:complexType>
  <xsd:attribute
      name="AttrOnNextLine"
      type="xsd:string"/>
  <xsd:element name=
      "ValueOnNextLine"
      type="xsd:string"/>
</xsd:schema>
